    "How would you explain, step by step, how to find the stationary points of an equation y=f(x)?": "To find stationary points, take the derivative f’(x) of the function. Set f’(x) = 0 and solve for x. These x-values are critical points. Plug them back into f(x) to find the corresponding y-values. For example, if f(x) = x³ - 3x, f’(x) = 3x² - 3, so x = ±1 are stationary points.",
